---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import airport from '../../../data/airport-contract/results.json';
import benchmark from '../../../data/ledger-eval/results.json';

// This page is not an experiment, so it sits outside the src/content/lab schema.
// Numbers that come from files in this repository are read from those files. Everything taken from
// GitHub (pull requests, runs, comments, the ruleset) cannot be computed here, so each of those facts
// is dated by CHECKED and links to the item that shows it. Re-read them when CHECKED gets old.
const CHECKED = '15 November 2026';
const REPO = 'https://github.com/felipealves7/felipealveslab';
const pr = (n: number) => `${REPO}/pull/${n}`;
const issue = (n: number) => `${REPO}/issues/${n}`;

const contractRules = airport.runs[airport.runs.length - 1].checks.length;
const pageRuns = benchmark.runs.filter((r) => r.suite === 'legacy47');
const bestRight = Math.max(...pageRuns.map((r) => r.rightOnAllFour));
const bestTotal = pageRuns[0].questions;
const scoredRuns = benchmark.runs.length;
---
<Base
  title="How the Lab is built — Felipe Alves Lab"
  description="How Felipe runs the Lab: he sets the direction, the rules and the acceptance bar; AI agents build to spec; every change ships through a checked pull request."
  ogType="article"
  css={['styles', 'responsive', 'enhancements', 'site-fixes', 'lab', 'lab-proof', 'lab-methodology']}
  bodyClass="case-page method-page"
  script="script"
  current="lab"
>
  <main id="method">
    <nav class="section-shell lab-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Felipe Alves</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/lab">Lab</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">How it's built</span></nav>

    <section class="section-shell method-hero" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <span class="eyebrow">Behind the Lab / Operating model</span>
      <h1 id="method-title">I set the direction.<br /><em>Agents build to spec.</em></h1>
      <div class="method-hero-bottom">
        <p class="method-hero-lede">I designed this Lab as a working model of AI-assisted delivery. I choose the questions, set the rules and the acceptance bar, and decide what is published. AI agents build to that specification: code, tests, pull requests and a first review. This page shows the operating model and the public record behind it.</p>
        <div class="method-margin-note"><span>Working rule</span><strong>Output is not evidence until someone checks it.</strong><small>Record checked {CHECKED}</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-dark-band" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
      <div class="section-shell method-band-inner">
        <span class="eyebrow">01 / Who does what</span>
        <h2 id="roles-heading">The agents build.<br />I decide what ships.</h2>
        <p>The aim is a repeatable delivery model: specify the problem, hand the build to agents, inspect the evidence and decide what is published.</p>
        <div class="method-roles">
          <article><span>Me / Direction</span><h3>Question, rules, acceptance</h3><p>I choose the problem and the data, set the rules the agents work under (<code>CLAUDE.md</code>), approve each build with the <code>go</code> label and merge what meets the bar.</p></article>
          <article><span>Claude / This website</span><h3>Build and integrate</h3><p>Claude Code works in this repository on <code>claude/</code> branches: Astro pages, pipelines, tests, fixes and the pull request. It reviews work handed in from outside before porting it.</p></article>
          <article><span>Other AI tools / Outside the repo</span><h3>Analysis packages</h3><p>Separate tools build analyses and evaluations elsewhere and hand over a package. The flight-reliability study and the Ask the Ledger evaluation arrived this way. The repository holds only what was ported.</p></article>
          <article><span>Automation / Scripts</span><h3>Checks without a person</h3><p>GitHub Actions build the site, run the tests and repository checks, run a weekly data check, run model benchmarks on demand and keep session links out of public text. They are scripts, not agents.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell method-section" aria-labelledby="controls-heading">
      <div class="method-section-top"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Controls register</span><h2 id="controls-heading">Each control, and the evidence that it operates.</h2></div>
      <p class="method-intro">Each row names a control, where it is written and what the public record shows, checked {CHECKED}.</p>
      <table class="decision-table method-table">
        <caption class="method-table-caption">Controls in this repository, with the evidence for each.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Control</th><th scope="col">Written in</th><th scope="col">What the record shows</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">No change reaches <code>main</code> without a pull request</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/rules/26100353`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ruleset <code>main-protected</code> ↗</a></td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">Active, with no bypass actors. Every change needs a pull request, a squash merge and passing <code>build</code> and <code>test</code> checks.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-enforced">Enforced</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">I approve each merge</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CLAUDE.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>CLAUDE.md</code> ↗</a>, rule 1</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">All 31 merged pull requests were merged from my account. Agents open pull requests; merging is my decision.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-owner">Owner review</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Build, tests and repository checks</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>ci.yml</code> ↗</a>, <code>scripts/check-content.mjs</code></td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">88 runs since 29 October 2026. They build the site, run the tests and check for employer names, secret-like strings and the required page sections.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-enforced">Enforced</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Session links kept out of issues and pull requests</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.github/workflows/chat-privacy.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>chat-privacy.yml</code> ↗</a>, rule 8</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">103 runs, none failed. Links are removed within a minute of posting.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-auto">Automated</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Weekly data check</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.github/workflows/airport-contract.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>airport-contract.yml</code> ↗</a>, Mondays 03:17 UTC</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">Passed on schedule on <a href={`${REPO}/actions/runs/41436558349`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2 November ↗</a> and <a href={`${REPO}/actions/runs/42611777794`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">9 November ↗</a>. 5 runs in all, none failed.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-auto">Automated</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Scout proposes projects</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.claude/prompts/scout.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>scout.md</code> ↗</a>, weekly on Monday</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">Reports on <a href={`${issue(10)}#issuecomment-6491403967`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">29 October ↗</a> and <a href={`${issue(29)}#issuecomment-6570113360`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2 November ↗</a>, with proposals #8, #9, #10 and #29. It adds nothing new while five proposals wait for my decision.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-evidenced">Evidenced</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Builder builds approved proposals</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.claude/prompts/builder.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>builder.md</code> ↗</a>, starts on the <code>go</code> label</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">Built issue #8 into <a href={pr(11)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #11 ↗</a> and issue #12 into the live Ask the Ledger box. Its stop rule held on issue #10, where the result missed the acceptance floor.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-evidenced">Evidenced</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Critic reviews pull requests</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.claude/prompts/critic.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>critic.md</code> ↗</a></td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">27 pull requests reviewed against a written checklist. In 9 of them the first review held the merge.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-evidenced">Evidenced</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" data-label="Control">Keeper maintains what is published</th>
            <td data-label="Written in"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/.claude/prompts/keeper.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><code>keeper.md</code> ↗</a>, weekly on Thursday</td>
            <td data-label="What the record shows">Raised maintenance issue <a href={issue(34)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#34 ↗</a> on 5 November 2026. It posts only when something needs doing.</td>
            <td data-label="Status"><span class="method-status is-evidenced">Evidenced</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="method-fineprint"><strong>Enforced:</strong> GitHub blocks the action. <strong>Automated:</strong> a workflow runs on every event or schedule. <strong>Owner review:</strong> my decision, recorded on each pull request. <strong>Evidenced:</strong> the agent's output is in the public record. Counts come from GitHub as of {CHECKED}; open the linked items to check them.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell method-section" aria-labelledby="exhibits-heading">
      <div class="method-section-top"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Three exhibits</span><h2 id="exhibits-heading">Three experiments, each with its evidence.</h2></div>
      <div class="method-evidence-grid">
        <article class="method-evidence-card">
          <div class="method-card-top"><span>Data engineering</span><span>Scheduled runs</span></div>
          <h3>Airport data with a written contract</h3>
          <p>A pipeline checks public airport, runway and country files against <strong>{contractRules} written rules</strong> every Monday. It passed on schedule on 2 and 9 November 2026. Each run is saved on the <code>airport-runs</code> branch, including a failure staged on purpose to prove the gate turns red.</p>
          <p class="method-card-limit"><strong>Shows:</strong> data contracts, scheduled validation and a gate that stops bad data.</p>
          <div class="method-card-links"><a href="/lab/airport-data-contract" aria-label="Open the airport data contract exhibit">Open exhibit</a><a href={`${REPO}/actions/runs/42611777794`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Scheduled run ↗</a><a href={`${REPO}/tree/airport-runs`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Saved results ↗</a></div>
        </article>
        <article class="method-evidence-card">
          <div class="method-card-top"><span>Analytics handover</span><span>Merged</span></div>
          <h3>Flight reliability</h3>
          <p>The analysis was built as a standalone project and handed over as a package. <a href={pr(27)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #27 ↗</a> ported its saved outputs and code on 1 November 2026. The site recomputes every figure, and the build stops if one disagrees. <a href={pr(28)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #28 ↗</a> then linked the Tableau Public dashboard and the Kaggle notebook after a signed-out check.</p>
          <p class="method-card-limit"><strong>Shows:</strong> analytics handover, reproducible figures and a build that checks them.</p>
          <div class="method-card-links"><a href="/lab/aviation-reliability" aria-label="Open the flight reliability exhibit">Open exhibit</a><a href={pr(27)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Integration PR ↗</a><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/data/aviation-reliability/external.json`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Dated check ↗</a></div>
        </article>
        <article class="method-evidence-card">
          <div class="method-card-top"><span>Conversational BI</span><span>Benchmark run</span></div>
          <h3>Ask the Ledger</h3>
          <p>The best of {scoredRuns} scored model runs answered <strong>{bestRight} of {bestTotal}</strong> questions right on all four synthetic ledgers. Adversarial testing found two queries that got past the live box's SQL check, one returning every row and one that never stops; <a href={pr(30)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #30 ↗</a> closed both. <a href={pr(31)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #31 ↗</a> made the benchmark a repeatable run.</p>
          <p class="method-card-limit"><strong>Shows:</strong> conversational BI, model evaluation and SQL guardrails.</p>
          <div class="method-card-links"><a href="/lab/ask-the-ledger" aria-label="Open the Ask the Ledger exhibit">Open exhibit</a><a href={pr(30)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Validator fix ↗</a><a href={pr(31)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Benchmark run ↗</a></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="method-lessons" aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
      <div class="section-shell method-lessons-inner">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">04 / How the system improves</span><h2 id="limits-heading">When the record shows a pattern, the rules change.</h2></div>
        <div class="method-lessons-copy">
          <div>
            <h3>Recurring problems are fixed in the rules.</h3>
            <p>On 29 October one cause accounted for 8 of 10 review holds. I changed the rules instead of patching each pull request: <a href={pr(19)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #19 ↗</a> added an automatic clean-up step and a one-pull-request-per-issue rule.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>The acceptance bar holds.</h3>
            <p>Issue #10 set a 70% accuracy floor for a tagger that separates airports named after people from those named after places. The Builder's second version scored 62.5% on a hand-labelled sample, so it opened no pull request and <a href={`${issue(10)}#issuecomment-6491583207`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">returned the decision to me ↗</a>. Nothing below the bar was published.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Credentials stay out of chats and files.</h3>
            <p>Model benchmarks run as a manual GitHub Actions job with repository secrets, so no token sits in a chat or a file. The first six runs were scored on 3 November 2026 (<a href={pr(33)} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PR #33 ↗</a>).</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Three layers before anything ships.</h3>
            <p>Automated checks gate the merge, the Critic reviews against a written checklist, and I make the final call.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-shell method-section method-source-section" aria-labelledby="sources-heading">
      <div class="method-section-top"><span class="eyebrow">05 / Inspect it yourself</span><h2 id="sources-heading">Claims with a trail.</h2></div>
      <p>Everything above links to a file, a pull request, a comment or a workflow run, and the counts are dated {CHECKED}.</p>
      <div class="method-source-links">
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CLAUDE.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>Rules</span><strong>CLAUDE.md: what agents may and may not do</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/.claude/prompts`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>Roles</span><strong>Scout, Builder, Critic, Keeper prompts</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/.github/workflows`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>Automation</span><strong>The workflows</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${REPO}/pulls?q=is%3Apr+label%3Aagent-built`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>History</span><strong>Every agent pull request</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${REPO}/rules/26100353`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>Gate</span><strong>The ruleset on main</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${REPO}/actions`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><span>Runs</span><strong>Recorded workflow runs</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="method-takeaway">
        <h3>What this demonstrates.</h3>
        <p>How I run AI-assisted delivery: frame the problem, set the guardrails, read the evidence and decide what ships.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="method-next"><div><span class="eyebrow">Back to the work</span><h3>See what the system has shipped.</h3></div><a class="button primary" href="/lab">Explore the Lab</a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
